/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/H2Ala-formation.dat -- the L-alanine master as the sum of its fully dissociated form (the inverse of the records written from the master; a case declares one master and the closure activates the record reachable from it):
      Ala(-1) + 2 H+  <=>  H2Ala

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 2.340, dH1 = 3.01 kJ/mol
      pK2 = 9.870, dH2 = 45.23 kJ/mol
  Source: Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049; H+(aq) = 0, zero ionic strength, aqueous species at 1 mol/dm3 (Table 1 caption, p. 1052).
  This record carries the sum of the first 2 steps (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species H2Ala; masters ( { ion Ala; nu 1; } { ion H; nu 2; } );
      logK25 12.21; dH -48240; source "Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049 -- Table 6, p. 1057: pK1 2.340, dH1 3.01 kJ/mol (read from a page image), pK2 9.870, dH2 45.23 kJ/mol (read from a page image) (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
